    <string name="termux_boot_help_summary">Learn how to add boot scripts</string>
    <string name="termux_api_help_content">Termux:API provides commands to access Android features from the terminal. Common commands:\n\n• termux-battery-status — battery info\n• termux-camera-photo — take a photo\n• termux-clipboard-get / termux-clipboard-set — clipboard\n• termux-notification — post a notification\n• termux-toast — show a toast\n• termux-vibrate — vibrate device\n• termux-location — get GPS location\n• termux-sms-list / termux-sms-send — SMS\n• termux-tts-speak — text to speech\n• termux-wifi-connectioninfo — WiFi info\n\nInstall the termux-api package first:\npkg install termux-api</string>
    <string name="termux_boot_help_content">Termux:Boot runs scripts automatically when the device starts.\n\nTo add a boot script:\n\n1. Create the directory:\n   mkdir -p ~/.termux/boot\n2. Place executable scripts in ~/.termux/boot/\n3. Scripts run in sorted order on boot.\n\nExample (~/.termux/boot/start-ssh):\n   #!/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/sh\n   termux-wake-lock\n   sshd</string>
